    "The fourth reaction is Biotite to Muscovite (KAl2(AlSi3O10)(F,OH)2).",
    "The fifth reaction is Muscovite to Quartz (SiO2).",
    "The Bowen reaction sequence is used to determine the temperature and pressure conditions under which igneous rocks formed.",
    "It is used to identify the minerals present in an igneous rock and their relative abundance.",
    "It helps reconstruct the cooling history of a magma chamber.",
    "It aids in understanding the geochemical evolution of magmatic systems.",
    "The temperature range for the Bowen reaction sequence is 1200°C to 600°C.",
